{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794045735,"nonce":"XhCR1Pj6Lw09oKeU+F1KvhgTzsI=","title":"Prepare ashui to compile and run on Rayzor","message":"Goal: ashui apps build with `rayzor` (JIT/AOT, later wasm) next to Ash/HashLink and Caribou. Nothing here is built yet; this is the plan agreed with the rayzor session (rayzor-a3) on the facts below.\n\n**Constraints**\n\n- Rayzor has no GC; memory is freed by static ownership and drop insertion. Its HDLL loading is experimental and does not account for GC, so blinc_abi.hdll via @:hlNative is not the route.\n- The route is a native plugin, like the Caribou adapter: blinc_abi gains a third feature on Rayzor's plugin ABI (plugin/src/lib.rs, ABI_VERSION handshake, declare_native_methods!, rpkg), and the externs in haxe/ashui/core/externs get a -D ashui_rayzor branch beside the ashui_caribou one (Handles, BlincNative, LayoutTreeNative, CssNative, TextNative, BitmapNative, SvgNative; about 150 functions).\n- Rayzor's wasm host links plugins as rlibs with the same extern \"C\" surface, so one plugin can serve native and wasm. Native first.\n\n**Native dependencies**\n\n- blinc_abi: layout, CSS, text, display list, hit testing, SVG, bitmaps, fonts, signals. Needs the Rayzor plugin adapter.\n- GPU: ashui imports gpu.* (hlwgpu, 151 classes). rayzor-gpu ships rayzor.gpu.* (155 classes, same xgpu API, own plugin package at rayzor/gpu). Needs an alias or shim, and a check that it covers render pipelines, bind groups, texture copies with row layouts, surface configure with desiredMaximumFrameLatency, and the hxsl-generated shaders.\n- Window: ashui imports window.* (hlwindow, from xwindow). rayzor/window is a hand-written crate today; the xwindow-based Rayzor window exists but its Haxe is not generated. Needs the generated window Haxe before any window runs.\n- Shaders: 13 UiShader classes use hxsl through hlwgpu.hxsl.Shader (caribou.hxsl.Shader under Caribou). Rayzor has its own @:shader lowering. Open: which one ashui uses there.\n- Macros: tink_hxx, ashui.ui.Markup, UiFramework.register, Assets.embed, CSS checks (23 files). Verified by rayzor-a3 for the editor only: the macro interpreter types the Pocket Studio demo (13 files) with 0 diagnostics in `rayzor lsp`. Not tested through a full build and codegen.\n- Others: hlavi media, ash.Future (async), ash-simd, native menu and file dialogs, threads, the wasm side module. Not yet evaluated.\n\n**Risks, in order**\n\n1. Memory model. Ashui's reactive graph keeps closures in long-lived signals and effects, and owner trees have parent/child cycles. rayzor-a3: values captured by a closure count as escaping; passing to a retaining callee, storing into a static, or storing via a non-variable right-hand side have uncovered paths, one confirmed as wrong results (aliasing); a cycle leaks until exit at best and is use-after-free at worst; Rc/weak annotations parse but are unproven. No program of this kind runs today. Mitigation: keep long-lived reactive state in the native plugin and Haxe objects short-lived, after a reduced signal/effect graph is run on Rayzor and checked.\n2. Callbacks. The ABI has native-callback futures settled once, and no general \"Rust calls a Haxe closure repeatedly\" hook. Host effects (a signal changes, Rust calls Haxe) need an ABI addition or a poll/queue pattern from the Haxe side. Needs the owner of plugin/ and runtime/.\n3. hl.* types: 223 uses of hl.Bytes, plus hl.Abstract, hl.Gc, hl.Ref, hl.Api. Rayzor core has Bytes, Ptr, Mem; whether they fit hl.Bytes access patterns is unchecked. Likely moves to haxe.io.Bytes at the extern boundary.\n4. Full-build macros. See above.\n\n**Phases**\n\n1. Smoke test: a small main importing ashui.ui.Component and one component, `rayzor check` with ashui's haxe/ on the class path; then widen until the first failures are listed. No Rayzor changes.\n2. Reduced reactive test: signals, computeds, effects and an owner tree with a cycle, run on Rayzor, results checked for leaks and aliasing. Decides where reactive state lives.\n3. Extern boundary: an ashui_rayzor branch in the externs and Handles; replace hl.Bytes at the boundary.\n4. blinc_abi Rayzor feature (plugin cdylib, rpkg), starting with layout tree, CSS and text; callbacks per risk 2.\n5. GPU: alias or shim for rayzor.gpu; the offscreen Snapshot path first (no window needed), then a window once its Haxe exists.\n6. Window, media, menu, async and SIMD, as each lands.\n7. wasm through Rayzor's host, after native.\n\n**Owners**\n\n- ashui session: phases 1 to 3, the externs, the issue.\n- rayzor-a3 (compiler/LSP): `rayzor check` findings, macro behaviour in a build. Will not change the ABI or ashui.\n- Rayzor plugin/runtime owner: callbacks, Bytes, handle ownership, memory model. Not yet identified.\n- blinc_abi owner (blinc session): the Rayzor feature.\n- Window Haxe generation: not yet owned.\n\n**Open questions**\n\n- Who owns Rayzor's plugin ABI and runtime, to answer callbacks, handle drops and string/buffer passing?\n- Does `rayzor build` survive ashui's macros (tink_hxx, Markup) through codegen?\n- Native or wasm first for the user? The plan assumes native.","files":null}]}